      "detail": "Opener: Tue 9/29 vs. Canadiens",
      "lotl": {
        "label": "What's Going On With the Leafs",
        "body": "A week of dress rehearsals has done what it was supposed to do: strip away the training-camp fog and show a team settling into its shape. <strong>The most telling development was Saturday's hospital visit in Arizona, where the Maple Leafs honored Matthew Mayich and reminded everyone that this club still carries a human pulse under the practice-ice routine.</strong> The on-ice numbers are tidy enough - two wins over Ottawa, 6-1 and 4-2, after those split-squad losses to Montreal - but the real story is the new season inching closer with Auston Matthews growing into the captaincy and the roster shaving down to business. <strong>Tuesday's opener against Montreal will finally tell us whether the Leafs' new edges hold when the games count for real.</strong>",
        "updated": "Updated September 27, 2026"
      },
