        "body": "The season has already turned rough, and the bruise is right there in the quarterback room - a 0-2 start, fourth in the NFC East, and a two-game skid that has left no room for spin. <strong>Jayden Daniels is out for Week 3 with an elbow injury, and Marcus Mariota is back under center</strong>; that is the headline, the wound, and the test all at once. Washington has been outscored and outmuscled, coughing up a 37-20 loss to Dallas after a 22-24 gut punch against Philadelphia. Daniels' injury strips the offense of its juice, and Mariota now has to steady a ship already taking on water. <strong>Next comes Seattle - and if the Commanders are going to stop the bleeding, it has to start there.</strong>",
