  "morning_brief": {
    "article": {
      "title": "Scherzer Starts Jays Finale as Leafs Visit Family",
      "paragraphs": [
        "Max Scherzer gets the ball this afternoon for the Blue Jays in the season finale against the Reds, with Toronto closing out at 3:07 p.m. ET on Sportsnet and Brandon Williamson on the other side. The Jays lost last night 5-1, and Scherzer said he wants to savor the moment with his future still undecided.",
        "The Leafs spent Saturday in Arizona visiting Matthew Mayich's family before practice at Arizona State, a quiet stop before Tuesday's season opener against the Canadiens at 7 p.m. ET on Sportsnet. The Raptors are still in camp, with a preseason game against the Heat set for Oct. 3, and the regular season opening Oct. 21 against the Bulls. The Commanders host the Seahawks today at 1 p.m. ET on FOX, with Marcus Mariota set to start and Jayden Daniels out because of an elbow injury."
      ]
    }
